[3b] Regression diagnostics (linearity, homoscedasticity, normality)...
  --- Regression diagnostics (autosomal training genes, Human HCT (Bartel)) ---
  Normality of TE (actual, log2 scale, n=10,640): skew = -0.019, excess kurtosis = 4.858, D'Agostino K^2 p = 9.22e-250, Jarque-Bera p = 0
  Normality of residuals: skew = -0.506, excess kurtosis = 3.515, D'Agostino K^2 p = 9.92e-279, Jarque-Bera p = 0
  Homoscedasticity (Breusch-Pagan): LM stat = 521.872, p = 2.15e-74
  Linearity (Ramsey RESET, power=3 on fitted values): F = 60.298, p = 9.14e-27
  (in each test, p < 0.05 => reject the null of normality / homoscedasticity / linearity)
